{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbdGwzZz4kDzQwtxoJKq", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7215, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16780, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7215}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "124ce361-dbe6-4215-b858-517821d86bc9", "uuid": "f7c4ead2-73bc-486b-8d85-13bac5d84000", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:51:19.973Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbdGwdV265VLiV74P9pM"}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbdGwzZz4kDzQwtxoJKq", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The main difference is that **lists are mutable and tuples are immutable**. Most of the other differences come from that.\n\n| | List | Tuple |\n|---|---|---|\n| Syntax | `[1, 2, 3]` | `(1, 2, 3)` or `1, 2, 3` |\n| Mutable? | Yes. You can append, remove or reassign items. | No. It's fixed once created. |\n| Hashable? | No | Yes, if all its elements are hashable |\n| Usable as dict key / set member? | No | Yes |\n| Methods | Many (`append`, `extend`, `insert`, `pop`, `remove`, `sort`, `reverse`, \u2026) | Only `count` and `index` |\n| Memory / speed | A bit larger, because it over-allocates to make appends cheap | Smaller, and slightly faster to create |\n\n```python\nnums = [1, 2, 3]\nnums[0] = 10        # fine\nnums.append(4)      # fine\n\npoint = (1, 2)\npoint[0] = 10       # TypeError: 'tuple' object does not support item assignment\n\nlocations = {(40.7, -74.0): \"NYC\"}   # tuple as a dict key: OK\nlocations = {[40.7, -74.0]: \"NYC\"}   # TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'\n```\n\n**Conventional usage:**\n- **List:** a collection of similar items whose length may change, like a list of users or a queue of tasks.\n- **Tuple:** a fixed group of values where each position has a meaning, like `(x, y)`, `(name, age)` or a function returning several values (`return total, count`). For readable field names, use `collections.namedtuple` or `typing.NamedTuple`.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- **Immutability is shallow.** A tuple can't be reassigned, but a mutable object inside it can still change. With `t = ([1], 2)`, `t[0].append(5)` works, and then `t` can't be hashed.\n- **A single-element tuple needs a trailing comma.** `(5)` is just the integer `5`, while `(5,)` is a tuple."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7215, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16780, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7215}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "124ce361-dbe6-4215-b858-517821d86bc9", "uuid": "0f9cd20a-b6b5-4895-9271-05acbdc932b4", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:51:26.153Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbdGwdV265VLiV74P9pM"}
